================================================================================
THIRD-PARTY DATA, EPHEMERIS & CARTOGRAPHIC CREDITS
================================================================================

1. NASA Goddard Space Flight Center (GSFC)
   - Besselian Elements, contact times, and Saros 126 ephemeris data
   - Credit: Fred Espenak & Jean Meeus, NASA Solar Eclipse Bulletins
   - Public Domain / U.S. Government Work

2. Xavier M. Jubier / International Astronomical Union (IAU)
   - High-precision TSE 2026 totality central line coordinates and local circumstance tables
   - Credit: Xavier M. Jubier (IAU Working Group on Solar Eclipses)
   - Used under scientific and educational research attribution

3. Astronomy Engine (Cosmonav / Don Cross)
   - High-precision vector calculations for Sun, Moon, and Earth orbital mechanics
   - Copyright (c) 2019-2024 Don Cross
   - MIT License

4. Three.js WebGL 3D Graphics Engine
   - 3D planetary rendering, camera controls, and custom shader pipelines
   - Copyright (c) 2010-2026 Three.js authors
   - MIT License

5. NASA Visible Earth (Blue Marble & Black Marble)
   - Global planetary surface textures and night illumination maps
   - Credit: NASA Goddard Space Flight Center / NASA Earth Observatory
   - Public Domain

6. Natural Earth Cartographic Data
   - Coastline vectors, territorial borders, and geographic features
   - Public Domain
